# Git LFS policy for Unreal binary SOURCE assets. See wonderland/GAUNTLET.md.
#
# WHY THESE AND NOT MORE. This repository tracked no binary asset until Aura
# (the in-editor agent on the Windows workstation) began producing them.
# Unreal's editable source assets are .uasset and .umap -- large, opaque, and
# unmergeable, which is the case Git LFS exists for. They are also `lockable`:
# two agents editing one asset cannot be merged, so the lock is the merge.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: cooked output (.ubulk, .uexp, .pak -- never
# committed; Binaries/, Intermediate/, DerivedDataCache/, Saved/ are ignored),
# and the small text/PNG textures the generator synthesises at build time
# (produced on the build host, never committed). If the pipeline later imports
# .fbx / .glb source meshes, add them here BEFORE the first commit, not after.
#
# Text history is untouched: these rules apply to NEW paths going forward
# (`git lfs track`), never `git lfs migrate`.
*.uasset filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
*.umap   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text lockable
